      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אָחוֹת</span></big><sub>114</sub>  <strong>subst. fem.: irmã (</strong>fenício <span dir=\"rtl\">אחת</span>, aramaico <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחָת</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܚܳܬܳܐ</span>, árabe <span dir=\"rtl\">أُخْتٌ</span>, assírio <em>aḫâtu</em>; Dl <sup>W</sup>; etiópico እኅት; sabeu em nomes próprios <span dir=\"rtl\">אחֿתאמהו</span>; Os <sup>ZMG 1865, 273</sup><strong>)</strong>—estado absoluto <span dir=\"rtl\">אָ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.1\">2 S 13:1</a> + (nunca com artigo); estado construto <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 4:22\" href=\"/Genesis.4.22\">Gn 4:22</a> +; com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחֹתִי (אֲחוֹתִי)</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 12:13\" href=\"/Genesis.12.13\">Gn 12:13</a> +, etc.; plural com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">אַחְוֹתַי</span> (qerê <span dir=\"rtl\">אַחְיוֹתַי</span>) <a data-ref=\"Joshua 2:13\" href=\"/Joshua.2.13\">Jos 2:13</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחוֹתַיִךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:51\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.51\">Ez 16:51</a> (qerê; ketiv <span dir=\"rtl\">אחותך</span>) + 2 ocorrências (Co propõe, para todas as ocorrências, ler <span dir=\"rtl\">אחיו׳</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">אַחֲיוֹתֵךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:52\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.52\">Ez 16:52</a> (Co propõe <span dir=\"rtl\">־תיך</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחוֹתֵךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:52\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.52\">Ez 16:52</a> (deve ser plural, mas Co propõe eliminar); <span dir=\"rtl\">אַחְיֹתָיו</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 42:11\" href=\"/Job.42.11\">Jb 42:11</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחוֹתֵיכֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"Hosea 2:3\" href=\"/Hosea.2.3\">Ho 2:3</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אַחְיֹתֵיהֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:16\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.16\">1 Ch 2:16</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 1:4\" href=\"/Job.1.4\">Jb 1:4</a>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>irmã</em> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 4:22\" href=\"/Genesis.4.22\">Gn 4:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 12:13\" href=\"/Genesis.12.13\">12:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 12:19\" href=\"/Genesis.12.19\">19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 20:2\" href=\"/Genesis.20.2\">20:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 20:5\" href=\"/Genesis.20.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 20:12\" href=\"/Genesis.20.12\">12</a> (mesmo pai, mãe diferente); assim também <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 18:11\" href=\"/Leviticus.18.11\">Lv 18:11</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 22:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.22.11\">Ez 22:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:30\" href=\"/Genesis.24.30\">Gn 24:30</a><sup>(×2)</sup> +; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 2:4\" href=\"/Exodus.2.4\">Ex 2:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 2:7\" href=\"/Exodus.2.7\">7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 18:9\" href=\"/Leviticus.18.9\">Lv 18:9</a> (qualquer um dos genitores em comum); assim também <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 27:22\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.27.22\">Dt 27:22</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 6:7\" href=\"/Numbers.6.7\">Nu 6:7</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.1\">2 S 13:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:2\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.2\">2</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:4\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.4\">4</a> +, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 8:8\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.8.8\">Ct 8:8</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; invocada no lamento pelos mortos <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 22:18\" href=\"/Jeremiah.22.18\">Je 22:18</a>; = parente próxima <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:59\" href=\"/Genesis.24.59\">Gn 24:59</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:60\" href=\"/Genesis.24.60\">60</a> (ou porque Labão era proeminente? assim Di); mulher da mesma nacionalidade <a data-ref=\"Numbers 25:18\" href=\"/Numbers.25.18\">Nu 25:18</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Hosea 2:3\" href=\"/Hosea.2.3\">Ho 2:3</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  = amada <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:9\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.9\">Ct 4:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:10\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.10\">10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:12\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.12\">12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">5:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:2\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.2\">2</a> (quatro ocorrências ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּלָּה</span> <em>noiva;</em> a expressão sugeriria que, originalmente, era permitido o casamento com meia-irmã — por parte de pai? cf. Nö<sup>ZMG 1886, 150</sup>; e <a data-ref=\"Genesis 20:12\" href=\"/Genesis.20.12\">Gn 20:12</a>).<br><strong>3.</strong>  simbolicamente, de Judá, Samaria, Sodoma e Jerusalém <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 3:7\" href=\"/Jeremiah.3.7\">Je 3:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 3:8\" href=\"/Jeremiah.3.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 3:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.3.10\">10</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:45\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.45\">Ez 16:45</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:52\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.52\">52</a>,<sup>(×2)</sup> (Co propõe eliminar) +; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.4\">23:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.11\">11</a> +.<br><strong>4.</strong>  figuradamente, de uma relação íntima <span dir=\"rtl\">אִמִּי וַאֲחֹתִי לָרִמָּה</span> … <span dir=\"rtl\">קָרָאתי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 17:14\" href=\"/Job.17.14\">Jb 17:14</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֱמֹר לַחָכְמָה אֲחֹתִי אַתְּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 7:4\" href=\"/Proverbs.7.4\">Pr 7:4</a>.<br>†<strong>5.</strong>  <em>outra</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אִשָּׁה אֶל־אֲחֹתָהּ</span>, a respeito das cortinas do tabernáculo <a data-ref=\"Exodus 26:3\" href=\"/Exodus.26.3\">Ex 26:3</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 26:6\" href=\"/Exodus.26.6\">6</a>, das alças, versículo <a data-ref=\"Exodus 26:5\" href=\"/Exodus.26.5\">5</a>, das espigas de encaixe, versículo <a data-ref=\"Exodus 26:17\" href=\"/Exodus.26.17\">17</a>; das asas dos seres viventes na visão de Ezequiel <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 1:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.1.9\">Ez 1:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 1:23\" href=\"/Ezekiel.1.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:13\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.13\">3:13</a>; não se usa a respeito de pessoas, mas ver <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, רְעוּת\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_רְעוּת\">רְעוּת</a>.",
